# Pyrokinesis divides a literal 4 among "any number of target creatures" (CR 601.2d): each target gets at least one, so
# a positive total needs at least one target and a board with no creature is no legal announcement (CR 601.2c). The
# offer used to skip divided slots altogether, so it said the cast was possible; a bot cast it, the division found
# nothing to aim at and quietly gave the cast up, and the bot cast it again for ever - a game that never moved, with
# nothing in the log and no prompt to anyone else.
#
# On turn 1 nothing is on the battlefield, so neither way to cast it is offered, though Lightning Bolt could pay the
# pitch cost. Once Bot2 has Llanowar Elves, the same pitch cast is offered and kills it.

[Bot1 Deck]
Pyrokinesis
Lightning Bolt
Mountain x5
Mountain x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Llanowar Elves
Forest x5
Forest x10

[Actions]
! Bot1.Hand.Pyrokinesis.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Pyrokinesis.Cast(Ability: Exile)

[Expect]
Turn = 3
Bot1.Graveyard = Pyrokinesis
Exile = Lightning Bolt
Bot2.Graveyard = Llanowar Elves
